  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Crate dependency direction",
      "items": [
        "bin-desktop → lib-desktop-<destination>-ui → lib-desktop-ui → lib-desktop-model → lib-ledger → domain crates → lib-core",
        "lib-desktop-navigation is gpui-free: the modal grammar router and the Intent enum, tested with plain #[test]",
        "lib-desktop-model depends on ports only (LedgerRepository, FileStore, ReplicaTransport); only bin-desktop links lib-database, lib-file-store and lib-sync-client and injects them at start-up",
        "Destination crates never depend on each other; they share Intents and actions through lib-desktop-ui (Zed's zed_actions pattern)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Data flow",
      "items": [
        "Keys: User → Shell → route_key → Intent → gpui action → Destination View (on_action)",
        "Clicks go straight to the element under the pointer and dispatch the same actions as keys",
        "A Dialog in the Chrome confirms with Apply(command) → ClientLedger runs it on the Ledger synchronously",
        "A landed command emits LedgerChanged naming its domains; Views re-read ClientLedger; a refusal emits nothing",
        "ClientLedger hands the drained LedgerChanges to a background task (write-behind); a failed write raises a Toast and reloads"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Replication (planned)",
      "items": [
        "The Sync Server holds a full replica of the Ledger database and Document files, not a change log",
        "Push: SyncReplicator takes a consistent SQLite snapshot (VACUUM INTO or the backup API) plus files and sends them through lib-sync-client",
        "Pull: download a replica, swap it in, then ClientLedger reloads through LedgerRepository::load()",
        "Open: the conflict and merge policy (last writer wins, single-writer lease, …) needs its own ADR, which also replaces Change Sets"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Crate names",
      "items": [
        "Destination UI crates: lib-desktop-dashboard-ui, -transactions-ui (with Import), -budgets-ui, -bills-ui, -documents-ui, -inventory-ui, -categories-ui, -tags-ui, -settings-ui",
        "Domain crates: lib-accounts, lib-bills, lib-budgets, lib-categories, lib-documents, lib-institutions, lib-inventory, lib-payees, lib-tags, lib-transactions, lib-units",
        "Proposed, marked (new) or \"new ·\" on the canvas: lib-desktop-ui, lib-desktop-navigation, lib-desktop-model, the destination crates, lib-file-store, lib-sync-client",
        "Renamed: LedgerStore → ClientLedger (GLOSSARY: a Client holds its own full local copy of the Ledger)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Configuration, Preferences, theme",
      "items": [
        "Configuration (lib-config) is read once in main into a read-only Global; the Locale is fixed for the run (ADR-0021)",
        "Ledger-scoped Preferences are Ledger data in ClientLedger, so they replicate with the database",
        "Client-scoped Preferences (Toasts on/off, ADR-0027), window and navigation state live in ClientState: never synced",
        "The Colours Global is derived from Configuration and both kinds of Preference and watched with observe_global"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "orange",
      "title": "Testing seams",
      "items": [
        "Pure crates (navigation, lib-ledger, domain crates, lib-core): plain #[test], no gpui linked",
        "lib-desktop-model: #[gpui::test] with TestAppContext and fake adapters behind a test-support feature",
        "UI: one headless test binary (ADR-0030) driving bin-desktop through VisualTestContext keystrokes and clicks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "slate",
      "title": "Notes",
      "items": [
